<section id="work" class="work"><div class="work-intro"><p class="eyebrow reveal">01 / WORK & EXPERIENCE</p><h2 class="reveal">Built for people.<br><em>Made to work.</em></h2><p class="work-description reveal">From logistics interfaces to payroll systems<br>and learning platforms. A few chapters so far.</p></div>
<article class="career"><div class="career-meta"><span>01 — LOGISTICS</span><span>2023 — PRESENT</span></div><div class="career-body"><div class="career-title"><h3 class="reveal">INFORM<span class="dot">.</span></h3><p>Frontend Software Engineer</p></div><div class="career-story"><p class="career-lead">Modern interfaces for<br>complex operations.</p><p>I rework legacy systems into web applications, building UI frameworks and internal tools for data-intensive logistics workflows.</p><details><summary>What I work on <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="details-content"><p>React interfaces, performance improvements, and reusable UI foundations that support complex business logic.</p><p>I also extend Java services, maintain Docker environments, and trace legacy C++ and Delphi code to understand the systems underneath.</p></div></details><div class="tech-list"><span>TypeScript</span><span>React</span><span>Java</span><span>GraphQL</span></div></div></div></article>
<article class="career"><div class="career-meta"><span>02 — HR SOFTWARE</span><span>2019 — 2022</span></div><div class="career-body"><div class="career-title"><h3 class="reveal">Campus<span class="serif">HR</span></h3><p>Full-stack Lead Developer & Architect</p></div><div class="career-story"><p class="career-lead">From business rules<br>to a working product.</p><p>I led the design and development of an HR SaaS platform, covering payroll, leave, documents, and employee tools.</p><details><summary>A closer look <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="details-content"><p>Built a flexible DSL-based calculator for payroll formulas and designed event-driven processing for large payroll batches.</p><p>Led developers and QA engineers, translated Chilean labour requirements into software, and worked directly with clients and sales.</p></div></details><div class="tech-list"><span>React</span><span>GraphQL</span><span>Prisma</span><span>Docker</span></div></div></div></article>
<article class="career"><div class="career-meta"><span>03 — LEARNING & MEDIA</span><span>2016 — 2022</span></div><div class="career-body"><div class="career-title"><h3 class="reveal">Campus<span class="serif">Chile</span></h3><p>Head of Technology</p></div><div class="career-story"><p class="career-lead">Where software<br>meets storytelling.</p><p>I looked after the technology behind an e-learning company, from platforms and infrastructure to interactive educational content.</p><details><summary>Across the whole process <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="details-content"><p>Managed and customised Moodle platforms, built dashboards and web tools, and maintained Ubuntu and DigitalOcean environments.</p><p>Wrote scripts, filmed and edited course videos, and led designers creating multimedia learning modules.</p></div></details><div class="tech-list"><span>Full-stack</span><span>Moodle</span><span>Infrastructure</span><span>Creative direction</span></div></div></div></article>
<div class="work-end"><p>Earlier: Developer Intern at Sigma Construcciones, 2015.</p><a class="text-link" href="Lucas-Pose-CV.pdf" download>Download my CV <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
<section id="about" class="about"><p class="eyebrow">02 / THE PERSON BEHIND THE WORK</p><div class="about-grid"><h2 class="reveal">Technical by trade.<br><em>Curious by nature.</em></h2><div class="about-copy"><p>I’m Lucas, a software engineer based in Santiago, Chile. I like finding the structure in complicated problems—and making the result feel natural to use.</p><p>My work has taken me from frontend systems and product architecture to filming and editing educational content. I enjoy having a foot in both worlds.</p><p>Outside of work: climbing, photography, guitar, and the occasional game of chess.</p><div class="education"><span>Computer Science Engineering</span><span>Pontificia Universidad Católica de Chile · 2022</span></div><a class="text-link" href="https://climatecare-archive.floating-berlin.org/2019/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Also made: Climate Care Archive <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section>
